1:# Agent Client Protocol
7:policy, read-only restrictions, tool authorization, verification, and receipt generation. ACP clients cannot change the
12:cancellation, streamed messages and tool updates, client-bound permission requests, and `_nexus/receipt/get`. The
17:## Declared limitations
23:- The receipt extension returns receipts retained by the current ACP connection. It is not a durable cross-connection
24:  receipt lookup API.

[
  {
    "schema_version": 1,
    "schemaSha256": "178eaba3c51574e25f72e22a41f79a64ca8e1ed98417df2c8a7fcbfd69c789b6",
    "note": "First published schema of the messages of the ACP adapter (AC-1), generated from AcpAdapterDocument in cli/src/acp/types.ts on release/v1.3.0: what a client may send that Nexus acts on (initialize, session/new, session/load, session/prompt, session/cancel, $/cancel_request, _nexus/receipt/get, and the reply to session/request_permission) and what Nexus sends (results, errors, session/update with agent_message_chunk, user_message_chunk, tool_call, tool_call_update and session_info_update, and session/request_permission). It describes Nexus's subset of the Agent Client Protocol version 1 plus Nexus's own extension method and _meta members, not ACP itself. Nothing was published before it. Types and pure functions only in this change: no command speaks these messages yet. Experimental: names and fields may change, each change with an entry here."
  }
]
[
  {
    "protocol": 1,
    "schemaSha256": "b2747ba8d5d56e8450df9c161b1c773b7beefd5c79ccd75fa07dfccda169b66a",
    "note": "First published schema of protocol v1, generated from cli/src/protocol.ts as it stood on release/v1.3.0. No wire change."
  },
  {
    "protocol": 1,
    "schemaSha256": "9cf30b58fb0f720ef8ecbf5f1a3d8ad5015ca0f842fee9131b9f7b4d017bb4bc",
    "note": "Add objective tool invocation budget exhaustion and accounting fields to turn results; additive protocol v1 change."
  },
  {
    "protocol": 1,
    "schemaSha256": "ec987e1083659ed595b68edea6f1707746fce82f6136ab7cc197d9dfa4d51037",
    "note": "Capability negotiation, additive, so the version stays 1. hello gains the optional fields protocol_min, protocol_max, capabilities and experimental; the new command initialize is answered by the new event initialized; error codes UNSUPPORTED_PROTOCOL and EXPERIMENTAL_DISABLED are added. An older client ignores the new hello fields and never sends initialize, so it sees what it saw before; a newer client that finds no range in hello falls back to the exact-version check, and one that sends initialize to an older sidecar gets BAD_REQUEST (unknown message type) and carries on without negotiation. No existing field or message changed meaning."
  },
  {
    "protocol": 1,
    "schemaSha256": "8db364275bdc319ad41f8f6896a9e4f68a79555a8b3b1999194c3118d216c4b5",
    "note": "Clarify verifier input binding in the protocol documentation. Description-only schema change; the wire shape and meaning are unchanged, so protocol stays 1."
  },
  {
    "protocol": 1,
    "schemaSha256": "2417ecafee1ba9f5a6d953caf063dac8b48ae6142d84a8260ad12c48f9540809",
    "note": "Add additive history tool-result metadata for complete ACP session/load replay; protocol stays 1."
  }
]

